                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pangas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a4281e1-e0e7-39cb-a8eb-f9bdb0d669f5",
                        "entry_id": "627f3786-78b8-3644-9330-01220b01f61c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Poisson d’élevage vietnamien, proche du poisson-chat, synonyme de poisson-chat du Mékong."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33f7cfe6-ba11-407b-817f-bcadbc19cc3e",
                                "sense_id": "7a4281e1-e0e7-39cb-a8eb-f9bdb0d669f5",
                                "text": "Le panga, poisson-chat originaire du Mékong et régions asiatiques proches, a une chair ferme et très parfumée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cec51bef-ffc2-4b10-9d96-7087544543bc",
                                "sense_id": "7a4281e1-e0e7-39cb-a8eb-f9bdb0d669f5",
                                "text": "Cela tombe bien, le panga est vendu à un prix modique (la moitié de celui du cabillaud, par exemple) et semble une ressource inépuisable."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2208d5de-a56c-4ad9-a3d4-8130a7d0c52d",
                        "source_entry_id": "627f3786-78b8-3644-9330-01220b01f61c",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a4281e1-e0e7-39cb-a8eb-f9bdb0d669f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "panga",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "panga",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7f7dd7f-cbc8-35f3-9022-9261b0554c7b",
                                        "entry_id": "b9ab410e-12a7-374b-a5cd-e2a846370104",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large broad-bladed knife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Africa",
                                            "East",
                                            "South-Africa"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a97fcb62-a086-488c-a447-089e2dbbc48e",
                                                "sense_id": "e7f7dd7f-cbc8-35f3-9022-9261b0554c7b",
                                                "text": "She turned to the small basket she was carrying and took out a panga."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "072bff8c-eff3-40c5-9ab6-82d84487a64c",
                                                "sense_id": "e7f7dd7f-cbc8-35f3-9022-9261b0554c7b",
                                                "text": "Charlie had told me what it had looked like immediately after the riots. Bodies hacked to pieces with pangas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95d88e32-04e8-4301-9cc6-60ab26909661",
                                                "sense_id": "e7f7dd7f-cbc8-35f3-9022-9261b0554c7b",
                                                "text": "I pleaded with them to lay down their arms, to take each other's hands in peace: ‘Take your guns, your knives and your pangas, and throw them into the sea!’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "panga",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "778114c8-9f62-317d-a9cc-960a068fbde2",
                                        "entry_id": "e3958844-e240-386f-9081-49940684e995",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various edible freshwater fish of the genus Pangasius, native to southeast Asia, especially an iridescent shark, Pangasius hypophthalmus, now reclassified as Pangasianodon hypophthalmus."
                                        ],
